    "body": "4.3 is maybe a bit difficult to read, maybe it can be worded better.\r\nIt essentially means that the reference child is kept even if the insertion target is adjusted.\r\nThis is needed for foster parenting + replace-with-children; with static sanitizer, foster parenting is done first, and then some parents are replaced with the final child order. But here, we insert directly into the final parent, so if the reference child was inserted first, that relationship needs to be kept.",
    "created_at": "2026-07-13T15:26:16Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-07-13T15:26:16Z",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/12645#discussion_r3571898750",
